  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Of the top 5 countries with the biggest economy in 2020, according to Madison Trust, which had coronary artery disease as the number one cause of death for males in both 2020 and 2021, according to the World Health Organization?",
  "answer": "Based on my research, here are the findings:\n\n## Top 5 Economies in 2020 (Madison Trust)\nAccording to Madison Trust's \"The 10 Biggest Economies in the World Over Time (1960-2024)\" page, the 2020 ranking is:\n1. **United States** — $20,936.6B\n2. **China** — $14,772.7B\n3. **Japan** — $5,064.9B\n4. **Germany** — $3,806.1B\n5. **United Kingdom** — $2,707.7B\n\nSource: [Madison Trust 2020 GDP ranking](https://www.madisontrust.com/information-center/visualizations/the-10-biggest-economies-in-the-world-over-time-1960-2024)\n\n---\n\n## WHO Cause-of-Death Data (Males)\n\n### 2020 (WHO Global Health Estimates 2021)\n| Country | #1 Cause of Death (Males) | IHD Rank |\n|---------|---------------------------|----------|\n| United States | **Ischaemic heart disease** (285.4k) | #1 ✓ |\n| China | Stroke (1,436.9k) | #2 |\n| Japan | **Ischaemic heart disease** (80.5k) | #1 ✓ |\n| Germany | **Ischaemic heart disease** (89.4k) | #1 ✓ |\n| United Kingdom | COVID-19 (45.3k) | #2 |\n\nSource: WHO GHE 2020 data — `https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/gho-documents/global-health-estimates/ghe2021_deaths_bycountry_2020.xlsx`\n\n### 2021 (WHO Global Health Estimates 2021)\n| Country | #1 Cause of Death (Males) | IHD Rank |\n|---------|---------------------------|----------|\n| United States | **Ischaemic heart disease** (289.1k) | #1 ✓ |\n| China | Stroke (1,437.2k) | #2 |\n| Japan | **Ischaemic heart disease** (85.3k) | #1 ✓ |\n| Germany | **Ischaemic heart disease** (91.2k) | #1 ✓ |\n| India* | COVID-19 (2,032.3k) | #2 |\n\nSource: WHO GHE 2021 data — `https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/gho-documents/global-health-estimates/ghe2021_deaths_bycountry_2021.xlsx`\n\n*India was not in the top 5 per Madison Trust (ranked 6th).\n\n---\n\n## Answer\n\n**Three countries** — **United States, Japan, and Germany** — had coronary artery disease (ischaemic heart disease) as the #1 cause of death for males in **both 2020 and 2021**, according to WHO data.\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n1. Madison Trust 2020 GDP ranking: https://www.madisontrust.com/information-center/visualizations/the-10-biggest-economies-in-the-world-over-time-1960-2024\n2. WHO GHE 2020 country data: https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/gho-documents/global-health-estimates/ghe2021_deaths_bycountry_2020.xlsx\n3. WHO GHE 2021 country data: https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/gho-documents/global-health-estimates/ghe2021_deaths_bycountry_2021.xlsx\n4. WHO GHO Leading Causes of Death portal: https://www.who.int/data/gho/data/themes/mortality-and-global-health-estimates/ghe-leading-causes-of-death",
